"Artikel: :ref:`Shading Language <doc_shading_language>`."

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:12
msgid "GLSL"
msgstr "GLSL"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:14
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rebel Shading Language is based on GLSL with the addition of a few quality-"
"of-life features. Accordingly, most features available in GLSL are available "
"in Rebel Shading Language."
msgstr ""
"Godot verwendet eine auf GLSL basierende Shader-Sprache mit einigen "
"verbesserten Funktionen. Dementsprechend sind die meisten in GLSL "
"verfügbaren Funktionen in Godots Shader-Sprache verfügbar."

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:19
msgid "Shader programs"
msgstr "Shader Programme"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:21
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In GLSL, each shader uses a separate program. You have one program for the "
"vertex shader and one for the fragment shader. In Rebel Engine, you have a "
"single shader that contains a ``vertex`` and/or a ``fragment`` function. If "
"you only choose to write one, Rebel Engine will supply the other."
msgstr ""
"In GLSL verwendet jeder Shader ein separates Programm. Sie haben ein "
"Programm für den Vertex-Shader und eines für den Fragment-Shader. In Godot "
"haben Sie einen einzelnen Shader, der eine ``vertex`` - und/oder eine "
"``fragment``-Funktion enthält. Wenn Sie nur eines schreiben, liefert Godot "
"das andere."

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:26
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rebel Shading Language allows uniform variables and functions to be shared "
"by defining the fragment and vertex shaders in one file. In GLSL, the vertex "
"and fragment programs cannot share variables except when varyings are used."
msgstr ""
"Mit Godot können einheitliche Variablen und Funktionen gemeinsam genutzt "
"werden, indem die Fragment- und Vertex-Shader in einer Datei definiert "
"werden. In GLSL können die Vertex- und Fragment-Programme nur dann Variablen "
"gemeinsam nutzen, wenn Variationen verwendet werden."

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:31
msgid "Vertex attributes"
msgstr "Vertex-Attribute"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:33
msgid ""
"In GLSL, you can pass in per-vertex information using attributes and have "
"the flexibility to pass in as much or as little as you want. In Rebel "
"Shading Language, you have a set number of input attributes, including "
"``VERTEX`` (position), ``COLOR``, ``UV``, ``UV2``, ``NORMAL``. For a "
"complete list, see the :doc:`Shading language reference </tutorials/shaders/"
"shader_reference/shading_language>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:40
#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:102
msgid "gl_Position"
msgstr "gl_Position (OpenGL)"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:42
msgid ""
"``gl_Position`` receives the final position of a vertex specified in the "
"vertex shader. It is specified by the user in clip space. Typically, in "
"GLSL, the model space vertex position is passed in using a vertex attribute "
"called ``position`` and you handle the conversion from model space to clip "
"space manually."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:47
msgid ""
"In Rebel Shading Language, ``VERTEX`` specifies the vertex position in model "
"space at the beginning of the ``vertex`` function. Rebel Engine also handles "
"the final conversion to clip space after the user-defined ``vertex`` "
"function is run. If you want to skip the conversion from model to view "
"space, you can set the ``render_mode`` to ``skip_vertex_transform``. If you "
"want to skip all transforms, set ``render_mode`` to "
"``skip_vertex_transform`` and set the ``PROJECTION_MATRIX`` to ``mat4(1.0)`` "
"in order to nullify the final transform from view space to clip space."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:57
#: tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:418
msgid "Varyings"
msgstr "Variiert"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:59
msgid ""
"Varyings are a type of variable that can be passed from the vertex shader to "
"the fragment shader. In modern GLSL (3.0 and up), varyings are defined with "
"the ``in`` and ``out`` keywords. A variable going out of the vertex shader "
"is defined with ``out`` in the vertex shader and ``in`` inside the fragment "
"shader."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:65
msgid "Main"
msgstr "Haupt"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:67
msgid ""
"In GLSL, each shader program looks like a self-contained C-style program. "
"Accordingly, the main entry point is ``main``. If you are copying a vertex "
"shader, rename ``main`` to ``vertex`` and if you are copying a fragment "
"shader, rename ``main`` to ``fragment``."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:75
msgid ""
"Global array constants are not supported in Rebel Shading Language. You can "
"fake the functionality by using a uniform initialized to the value, but you "
"will not benefit from the increased speed from using a constant."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:79
msgid "Macros"
msgstr "Makros"

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:81
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In keeping with its similarity to C, GLSL lets you use macros. Commonly "
"``#define`` is used to define constants or small functions. There is no "
"straightforward way to translate defines to Rebel Shading Language. If it is "
"a function that is defined, then replace with a function, and if it is a "
"constant, then replace with a uniform. For other macros (``#if``, "
"``#ifdef``, etc.), there is no equivalent because they run during the pre-"
"processing stage of compilation."
msgstr ""
"Entsprechend der Ähnlichkeit mit C können Sie mit GLSL Makros verwenden. Im "
"Allgemeinen wird ``#define`` verwendet, um Konstanten oder kleine Funktionen "
"zu definieren. Es gibt keine einfache Möglichkeit Definitionen in Godots "
"Shader-Sprache zu übersetzen. Wenn es sich um eine definierte Funktion "
"handelt ersetzen Sie sie durch eine Funktion. Wenn es sich um eine Konstante "
"handelt, ersetzen Sie sie durch ein Uniform. Für andere Makros (``#if``, "
"``#ifdef`` usw.) gibt es kein Äquivalent, da sie während der "
"Präprozessorphase der Kompilierung ausgeführt werden."

#: tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_rebel_shaders.rst:92
msgid ""
"GLSL has many built-in variables that are hard-coded. These variables are "
"not uniforms, so they are not editable from the main program."
msgstr ""
"GLSL verfügt über viele integrierte, fest codierte Variablen. Diese "
"Variablen sind keine Uniforms, daher können sie nicht vom Hauptprogramm aus "
"bearbeitet werden."

